!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/valid/the-kind-of-namespace-holds-the-namespace-types-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.1, [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    A reference over a constructor holds the entries whose value is of it. A namespace type is an instance of
    `meta.namespace`, so the fixture's `api` and `router` and the kernel's `meta.schema` are members of
    `meta.kind<meta.namespace>`, and so is the kernel root's `schema`, an alias of `meta.schema`, as a kind holds
    every alias of a member. `meta.namespace` itself is declared as a record, its value of `meta.record`, and is no
    member, and `meta.field_map` is an ordered map keyed by text, an instance of `meta.map`, and no member either.
    `myapi` and `routes` are values of `api` and `router`, which are no constructors, so they are no members.
    """
  valid: {
    members: [
      { name: namespaces  members: [api meta.schema router schema] }
    ]
  }
}
